  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PRM Voluntary Contribution to IOM Response Overview Sudan Crisis and Neighbouring Countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the outbreak of the conflict in Sudan on 15 April 2023, more than 2 million individuals crossed borders into neighbouring countries. In South Sudan, more than 675,353 individuals have crossed the borders into South Sudan (as of 29 May 2024) with an estimated 78 per cent being South Sudanese nationals returning to their areas of origin or relocation. The influx has remained consistent throughout the crisis with an average of 1,500 people arriving daily in South Sudan. As of April 2024, the Egyptian Ministry of Foreign Affairs reported that 514,827 individuals had crossed into Egypt from Sudan. Under this project, IOM is providing lifesaving, humanitarian and protection assistance to refugees, migrant returnees and third country nationals fleeing from the conflict in Sudan to the South Sudan and Egypt. The multi-sectoral response spanning several countries includes protection assistance, Displacement Tracking Matrix flow monitoring, mental health and psychosocial support, water, sanitation and hygiene assistance, and direct healthcare, among other assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
